A recommendation is a category-A-recommendation and is an evidence-type-4-recommendation.
Every clinician should evaluate a risk for an opioid-related-harm before an opioid-initiation.
Every clinician should evaluate a risk for an opioid-related-harm during a periodic-continuation-review.
Every clinician should discuss a risk for an opioid-related-harm with a patient.
Every clinician should incorporate a risk-mitigation-strategy in a management-plan with a patient and should offer a naloxone-dose.
